# The Solrise app revision the image should be built from.
#
# Why this file exists: the app is published as an *orphan* branch
# (`scripts/publish-app.sh` -> `solrise_erp-app`) whose root is the Frappe app.
# Such a branch carries no `.github/`, so a push to it can neither start a
# workflow nor check out a tree that could run one - publishing the app rebuilds
# nothing by itself, and the only other trigger is a hand-run
# `gh workflow run build-image.yml`.
#
# This file is the handshake that closes that gap: `build-image.yml` watches it,
# so recording the revision that was just published - together with what changed
# and why - is what asks CI to build. It also leaves the answer to "which app
# commit is in this image?" in the repository rather than in a shell history.
#
# Written by hand on purpose. A file the build *reads* should not also be a file
# some other process rewrites underneath it.
#
#   branch                                     commit
